Figure 1. From shared work to shared knowledge.
This engraving shows typesetting, printing, and proofreading as parts of a coordinated process. Books carry the result beyond the workshop, where others can learn from it and build on it. MASS draws on a related idea: a team's collective work can provide training examples for the model its members share.
Jan Collaert I, after Stradanus,
The Invention of Book Printing
